{{also|Rowan}}
==English==
[[File:Rowan tree 20081002b.jpg|right|thumb|A European rowan]]

===Etymology 1===
From Northern English or Scottish, of {{etyl|non|en}} origin: compare {{m|non|reynir}}; compare Norwegian {{m|no|rogn}}, Danish {{m|da|røn}}. Ultimately related to the root of {{m|en|red}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/rəʊən/|lang=en}}
* {{a|Northern England}}, {{a|Scotland}} {{IPA|/raʊən/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/roʊən/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|əʊən|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# ''[[Sorbus aucuparia]]'', the [[European rowan]].
# Any of various small [[deciduous]] [[tree]]s or [[shrub]]s of genus ''[[Sorbus]]'', belonging to the rose family, with [[pinnate]] leaves, [[corymb]]s of white flowers, and usually with orange-red berries.

